            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LazyJane"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am just trying it! What a great taste. Big thumbs-up from my husband. I didn't have fresh jalapenos on hand, so used a jar of pickled jalapenos. For fresh tomatoes, same thing; used a can of diced tamatoes. It was just great. I first put usual pepper but saw the black ground pepper notation and added that to the mix. What a difference it makes! \nSadly no more chips to scoop it up! This one will go into my recipe box."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "scooter"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My guests raved on this one. Did add 1 minced garlic clove, seeded the tomato, used lime instead of lemon. And mashed half the guac and left half in small cubes for that chunky texture.",
            "datePublished": "2013-03-19T07:56:10.200Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kychef69"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is by far the best guacamole recipe I've ever made!! I made a few minor changes.. Only did 1tbls of lemon juice and added juice of 1 1/2 limes and added 1clove mined garlic . Used previous suggestion and put avacado pit in finished product and it kept its color! Took this to work and everyone raved about it!! I also doubled the recipe so I had plenty left over to munch on!!",
            "datePublished": "2013-12-22T22:06:07.073Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alice McGill"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe!!! I’ve made it several times and have had compliments every time. I do use 4 avocados (instead of only 2), and use a half of a lemon for its juice, and sometimes I end up using all of the lemon juice, for an extra zing to the guac. But that’s just a preference. Overall I love that the lemon juice keeps the guacamole from turning brown.",
            "datePublished": "2019-10-22T17:54:16.190Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Roberta Rose"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Well I did want to make it last. I added 1/2 C of sour cream, and 1/2 C of cottage cheese. It makes a great dip this way!!",
            "datePublished": "2017-03-24T04:49:08.777Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MintPulp9375"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! I left the avocado chunky, rather than creamed, which can be slimy. I also deseeded the tomatoes and patted them dry with kitchen roll so that the mixture wouldn't get too soggy. I didn't have any limes to hand so had to use lemon but will make sure that I have limes for the next time I make this (and there will be a next time) as the flavour is different. I also used a milder red chilli, rather than a jalapeño as I didn't want to overwhelm the flavour of the avocados.",
            "datePublished": "2025-05-23T12:56:57.024Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Basically using the same recipe as yours except with lime instead of lemon. We always put a thin layer of mayonnaise over the top of the guacamole to keep it from turning colors. Just before serving we remove it from the fridge and stir the mayonnaise into the dip. It is excellent and even more creamy. This idea was in a cookbook called \"Tidewater on the Halfshell.",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-12T13:42:55.593Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shari"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Too much tomato, and you use LIME juice for authentic guacamole, not lemon juice. Also, don't overmash the avocados. They will become greasy, not creamy, since they are very high in natural oil. Instead, for a better texture, mash lightly with a fork, leaving the mixture fairly chunky.",
            "datePublished": "2021-02-02T20:38:48.990Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sharon Van Winkle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We love guacamole and this is a good recipe, but definitely use lime juice and add some garlic. A tip to keep your guacamole from turning brown is to put the avocado pits back into the guac until you are ready to serve.",
            "datePublished": "2013-08-16T10:37:52.683Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Patty in Dallas"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The only difference is that I use the juice of a fresh lime instead of lemon juice. I just like that particular citrus better with avocado. And I used 2 Florida avocados which are considerably larger than Haas so the amount of the other ingredients don't overshadow the avocado. This combination of flavors is a hit to all who have tried it. If you use Haas for this recipe, make sure you use at least 4 of them or cut down on the other ingredients in my opinion. Thanks for sharing Kaersten!",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-09T09:46:48.267Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used half lime juice and half lemon juice. Since this was for my Cinco de Mayo party, I added a little extra lemon juice to ensure the avocado didn't turn black before the party was over. It worked and the guacamole was a huge hit!",
            "datePublished": "2025-05-05T01:32:36.128Z"
          },
